WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.637
Idea. Think about a fridge at home stuffed with food. Some of it goes off before anyone eats it. That is waste: wasted food, wasted space and wasted money.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:24.283
Lean production means making goods with as little waste as possible: waste of materials, time, space and money. Inventory, or stock, is the materials and finished goods a business holds.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:39.199
Method. Just-in-time, or JIT, means materials arrive, or goods are made, only when they are needed. Look at these example figures: a business using JIT holds far less stock.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:52.911
Kaizen means continuous improvement. All employees regularly suggest small changes to how work is done. It can improve quality and cut waste, but it depends on staff being willing to take part.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:06.171
To answer any lean question, name the lean idea, say which waste it removes, then chain it to lower costs, better quality or higher productivity. Use the case product if a business is named.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:20.779
Worked example. Here is a real exam question from Paper two in June 2025. Explain one reason why many manufacturing businesses use just-in-time. It is worth three marks.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:27.748
Mark one is the reason. JIT cuts the amount of inventory a manufacturer holds.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:38.607
Mark two links it. Materials arrive only when they are about to be used, so less warehouse space is needed, and fewer materials go out of date or get damaged.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:52.671
Mark three gives the result. Storage and waste costs fall, so overall costs fall and the business can make more profit. This explanation is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:04.667
Common mistake. A common mistake is mixing up the two methods. JIT is about stock arriving when needed. Kaizen is about continuous small improvements.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:13.228
Another mistake is saying JIT means fast production. It means receiving or making stock only when it is needed.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:30.350
Your turn. Now you try. At a bicycle factory, workers meet every Friday to suggest small changes, such as moving tools closer to the assembly line. Which lean method is this? Give one benefit and one risk. Pause and decide.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:47.581
Answer. It is Kaizen: continuous small improvements suggested by the workers. Moving tools closer saves time on every bicycle, so productivity rises and costs fall. The risk: it only works if staff are willing to take part.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:59.071
Remember the method: name the lean idea, say which waste it removes, then link it to lower costs or better quality for the business. Now try the practice questions.
